nodecode-agenda-guardian is a rewrite of Moodtuner997's Moodtuner997/hermes-agenda-guardian:
  https://github.com/Moodtuner997/hermes-agenda-guardian
  commit 2493df2b4b85985faf7f19e4d9b6fe838b9ed5dd
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Moodtuner997 (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the rules a user writes once (work hours, workdays, protected windows, the focus window, the buffer, the longest block, the tasks a day) and the planner that obeys them; the estimate of each task and the correction of that kind's estimates by the median of the user's own finished times from the third finished task of the kind, said in the block's reason; the placement in the free time around a calendar's events, all-or-nothing per task, split into blocks no longer than the longest block and preferring the focus window; the day's text with a reason on every block and a "not placed" line for what does not fit, instead of an overbooked day. The reading of an .ics calendar (a file or an https address) is carried, with the original's rules about which addresses are accepted at all. The harness seams are Nodecode's: the section is the config, the tools and /agenda-guardian are one declaration, and the tasks, the rules changed in the chat and the finished times live in one JSON file in the folder the section names.

Left out, because they belong to the other harness or to a part of the original this rewrite does not carry: the dashboard tab (Nodecode has no such surface here), the two cron reminders the original schedules in its own harness, its pre-tool-call guard and its gateway hook, the Google Workspace write path (this cell never writes to a calendar), the JSON-file and command calendar sources, the week plan and the activity proposals drawn from eight weeks of calendar history, and the French texts. The event reader covers ordinary VEVENT start and end values, floating or with a Z; a recurring event is read at its first occurrence only.
